# Checks and Rolls

## Tier Bonus

Whenever you make an ability check, attack roll, or saving throw using a skill, tool, or weapon with which you have proficiency, you add your **tier bonus** to the d20 roll.

Your tier bonus is determined by your character level, as shown in the Character Progression table.

### Tier Bonus by Level

| Level | Tier Bonus |
|-------|-------------------|
| 1-4   | +2                |
| 5-8   | +3                |
| 9-12  | +4                |
| 13-16 | +5                |
| 17-20 | +6                |

### Stacking Tier Bonus

Your tier bonus can't be added to a single die roll more than once. Occasionally, your tier bonus might be multiplied or divided (such as halved for familiarity, or doubled for expertise) before applying.

If a feature says "add double your tier bonus," calculate the numeric value first: `tierBonus × 2`.
